ght political causes go back to  the book from the 1990s the foundations  of geopolitics where it  outlines Russia's strategies for  interfering in other countries including  in the US and it includes try to  escalate racial tensions a great way to  do that is by funding extreme right-wing  groups another way to do that which  Russia did in the United States was  geo-targeting people in Ferguson  Missouri and I believe it was in  Baltimore Maryland during the time of  unrest there what Russia is accused of  having done in the United States during  the 2016 election matches exactly with  what this report found that they did in  19 other countries over a two decade  period and at some point what's that  phrase if it looks like a duck if it  smells like a duck if it walks like a  duck quacks like a duck if it tastes  like a duck one might say although not  vegan appropriate it's probably a duck  at some point right or maybe there's the  new way to say it if you watch those CNN  commercials is an apple is an Apple no  matter what you call it not a banana  it's not a banana it's not an orange  it's not a persimmon even try persimmon  though it's a nice nice little fruit so  what we're learning is that the stunning  part isn't that someone would allege  Russia interfered in our election that  that's kind of the obvious part that's  the believable part the stunning part is  increasingly that anyone would think to  deny that Russia would have done this  and here's a quote from the report  nearly 20 years ago Vladimir Putin  gained and solidified power by  exploiting blackmail fears of terrorism  and war since then he has combined  military adventurism and aggression  abroad with propaganda and political  repression at home to persuade a  domestic audience that he is restoring  Russia to greatness and a respected  position on the world stage all the  while he has empowered the state  security services and employed them to  consolidate his hold on the levers of  political social and economic power  which he has used to make himself and a  circle of loyalists extraordinarily  wealthy you know in reading that it  feels a lot like what Donald Trump is  doing in the United States he is using  political power government power trying  to use legislative  judicial power to consolidate his status  and the status of his friends cronies  and family members and a bunch of the  people on his cabinet to become even  wealthier than they were going into this  entire thing what about what we can do  right that's the next question let's  assume that now I'm talking to the  reasonable people who understand  Russia's been doing this for decades  they did in the United States the exact  same thing that they did in other  countries for decades what can we do to  prevent them from continuing to do this  to our elections in the future very long  list the report includes something like  30 or more examples but a couple things  are number one sanctions sanctions do  work if they're appropriate if they are  strong enough and they are targeted in  the right way requiring disclosure by  social media platforms of who is funding  their political ads and that is a sort  of twofold effect if social media  platforms know that if they take this  foreign money it will be public  information they would be less likely to  do it and also to some degree it's  possible that the foreign powers if they  know that it will be public that they  bought ads and tried to exert influence  maybe they'd also be less likely to do  the ad buys although I think for Putin  he would love the idea of that going  public because the the goal is just to  create chaos but at least from the point  of view of Twitter if your Twitter and  you know in advance we accept this money  from the Russians it's gonna have to be  disclosed publicly we don't want to end  up testifying before Congress again  let's just refuse the money that  impossible  another thing would just be to not have  a deal financial 